# Finish with a pull request

When a development cycle is done (tests passing, ready to integrate), **push the branch and create a pull request**. Do not ask whether to merge locally, keep the branch, or discard.

- Push with `git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream.
- Open the PR with `gh pr create` against `main`.
- Do not merge locally, force-push, or delete the branch unless the user says so.
- Leave the working tree in place so PR review can continue.
